      "steps": [
        "At Zora Fountain bomb the rear rock wall; play Zelda’s Lullaby and pay 100 rupees for Farore’s Wind. Collect the high night token with the Boomerang before leaving.",
        "In the southeastern Hyrule Field marsh, bomb open the cracked-rock grotto and defeat the ordinary Skulltula inside while a child. This sets up an adult crate containing its Gold Skulltula; return in r24. Without the child kill, the adult crate will not appear.",
        "Sweep the Boomerang-only night pickups at Lake Hylia, Lon Lon Ranch and behind Dampe’s hut. Plant beans at the laboratory, Graveyard, Dodongo entrance, Kokiri shop soil and both Lost Woods soils after flushing their tokens with bugs.",
        "From the Lost Woods entrance go right, left, right, left, left; enter the butterfly-marked Forest Stage hole. Wear Skull Mask for the stick upgrade. Return to the entrance’s first-left Skull Kid, sell the mask, repay the shop and borrow Spooky Mask. Sell that to the Graveyard child by day, repay and borrow Bunny Hood.",
        "After all three Stones the Running Man is in Hyrule Field. Meet him when he stops to rest and sell Bunny Hood for the remake’s 200-rupee reward. Repay the mask shop to unlock Mask of Truth and the three cosmetic race masks. Borrow Mask of Truth, show it at the Forest Stage and speak to the leader for the nut-capacity reward.",
        "Bomb the boulder just outside the Sacred Grove for the other nut upgrade. In Goron City stop the large rolling Goron with a bomb in his tunnel for the other Bomb Bag upgrade. In Castle grounds visit the bombable fountain and pay 50 rupees for the magical spin enhancement, and complete the child fishing reward described in the attached collectible."
      ],
